<title>POLAND: POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 1.0 PCT IN MARCH 1-20-NBP.</title>
<headline>POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 1.0 PCT IN MARCH 1-20-NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by</p>
<p>1.36 billion zlotys, or one percent, in March 1-20 to 139.70</p>
<p>billion after a 1.6 pct rise in February, preliminary central</p>
<p>bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 2.8 percent in the January-March 20</p>
<p>period against 6.1 percent in January-March of 1996.</p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		    MARCH 1-20  FEB    MARCH 96</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)		1.0	1.6	 2.4</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   139.70   138.34    110.64</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	24.99    24.57     21.13</p>
<p>  National currency		     114.71   113.77     89.51</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    23.75    23.45     20.64</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    86.51    85.29     59.56</p>
<p>NOTE - revised figures in brackets</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
